{"title":"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A list of five numbers repeats to form the pattern\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/b/56b1a21e458415ac1902b9a9a19201385bc73105.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5, 6, 7, 8, 9, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9, \\cdots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"284\" height=\"17\" /></center>\n<p>What is the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/9/f490c9585fc04684a97f897f87d49d972658089a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$221$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /><sup>st</sup> number in the pattern?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/4/744813e9b381a8f78ba7586191db5a75cac5157e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 5 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 6 \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 7 \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 8 \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"351\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Slow.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Slow)\">Solution 1 (Slow)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Slow)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Writing all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/9/f490c9585fc04684a97f897f87d49d972658089a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$221$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> numbers, we see that the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/9/f490c9585fc04684a97f897f87d49d972658089a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$221$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /><sup>st</sup> number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/8/ad89ed6de49d089fcce622aa3dd3867c83445d9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf {(A) } 5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"58\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Faster.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Faster)\">Solution 2 (Faster)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Faster)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> numbers repeated, meaning that we can find the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/9/f490c9585fc04684a97f897f87d49d972658089a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$221$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /><sup>st</sup> number by finding the remainder when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/9/f490c9585fc04684a97f897f87d49d972658089a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$221$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/9/f490c9585fc04684a97f897f87d49d972658089a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$221$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> more than a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/9/f490c9585fc04684a97f897f87d49d972658089a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$221$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /><sup>st</sup> number is the same as the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /><sup>st</sup> number, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/8/ad89ed6de49d089fcce622aa3dd3867c83445d9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf {(A) } 5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"58\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)\" title=\"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)\">2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.p